@synopsis
**yumed-v2-reference** [ **--config** *path* ] [ *options* ]
**yumed-v2-reference** **completion** **bash**
**yumed-v2-reference** **--completion** **bash**
**yumed-v2-reference** **--help**
**yumed-v2-reference** **--version**
@end

## DESCRIPTION

**yumed-v2-reference** is the transport-v2 reference daemon. It listens for
authenticated YUME clients, validates their auth keys, negotiates transport
capabilities, and opens
outbound target sockets for allowed streams. It can also serve a real HTTP
facade for non-YUME requests, provide operator-authority proof and
privacy-minimizing logging, manage authorized keys, and expose relay/directory
features when enabled.

For an accepted 2.0 tunnel, yumed-v2-reference is the public TLS/HTTP/2 endpoint. A
separately supervised Node.js 24 process on loopback supplies the genuine cover
site and never receives tunnel records or secrets.

The product version is 0.3.0-dev1; this daemon speaks transport-v2 wire
0.2.0-dev6. AUTH v2 verifies composite Ed25519 and ML-DSA-87 client identities
bound to the live TLS exporter. ML-KEM-1024, X25519, and the random file PSK
contribute to establishment; an admin session requires a separate second
identity. The default native YTP/1 application and its schema-1 tools are
separate. A schema-1 configuration does not drive this daemon.

## BASIC SETUP

@code text
sudo yumed-v2-reference \
    --listen 443 \
    --cert /etc/yume/server.crt \
    --key /etc/yume/server.key \
    --auth-keys /etc/yume/authorized_keys \
    --obfs-secret-file /etc/yume/obfs.hex \
    --inner-psk-file /etc/yume/inner.hex \
    --real-backend loopback://127.0.0.1:3000
@end

Port 443 requires root or **cap_net_bind_service**. After binding, the daemon
can drop privileges unless **--root** is used.

