Worker thread count in the range 0..256. Use **0** for automatic selection.
@opt **--max-sessions** *n*
@cli spell: --max-sessions <N>
@cli help: Hard cap on simultaneously-tracked
@cli help: sessions. New accepts past the cap are
@cli help: closed immediately. 0 = unlimited.
@cli help: Default 256; 0 explicitly disables.

Hard cap on all simultaneously tracked sessions. Default 256. Use 0 only to
explicitly disable the cap.
@opt **--bulk-key-max-sessions** *n*
@cli spell: --bulk-key-max-sessions <N>
@cli help: Default concurrent sessions for each
@cli help: regular key marked key_type=bulk.
@cli help: Default 64; per-key max_sessions wins.

Default authenticated-session cap for each regular key marked
**key_type=bulk**. Default 64; per-key metadata may override it.
@opt **--rekey-window** *n*
@cli spell: --rekey-window <N>
@cli help: Concurrent directional epoch offers accepted
@cli help: per session, and the ceiling on this
@cli help: server's own sending window (1..64;
@cli help: default 8). Each prepared epoch adds
@cli help: one negotiated epoch budget per rekey
@cli help: round trip on high-latency links.

Concurrent directional epoch offers accepted from one session, and the ceiling
on this server's own sending window. Range **1**-**64**, default **8**. Each
prepared epoch adds one negotiated epoch byte budget per rekey round trip on
high-latency links; the value is advertised in the TLS-protected AUTH challenge
and bound into the signed transcript. It bounds how much ML-KEM work a peer can
request. Under the default Extreme mode the budget is 256 KiB, with independent
limits of 512 frames and 500 ms sender-active time. The JSON key
**security_mode** selects Extreme, Normal, Soft, or a complete bounded Ultimate
policy; see **docs/SECURITY_MODES.md**.
@opt **--accept-rate-limit** *n*
@cli spell: --accept-rate-limit <N>
@cli help: Cap on accepts per second over a 1 s
@cli help: shared accounting window. Refused accepts close
@cli help: immediately. 0 = unlimited.
@cli help: --public-node defaults to 100 when unset.

Maximum newly accepted TCP connections per second. Use 0 for unlimited.
@opt **--tls-handshake-timeout-ms** *ms*
@cli spell: --tls-handshake-timeout-ms <ms>
@cli help: Close the socket if the TLS handshake
@cli help: doesn't complete in this many ms.
@cli help: Slow-loris guard. 0 = no deadline
@cli help: --public-node defaults to
@cli help: 10000 when unset.

Abort slow TLS handshakes after *ms* milliseconds.
@opt **--egress-mbps** *n*
@cli spell: --egress-mbps <N>
@cli help: Weighted fair egress cap across identities.
@cli help: 0 = disabled. One active identity can use
@cli help: the full cap; equal identities split it.
@cli help: auth_keys_meta weight 0.1..100 controls
@cli help: weighted shares (default 1.0).

Aggregate weighted fair server egress cap in Mbit/s. Set it at or below the
real link limit. Active identities split the cap using metadata **weight**
values; every bulk-key session is a separate identity.
@opt **--reverse-port-min** *port*
@cli spell: --reverse-port-min <p>
