option is unavailable.
@end

## SECURITY OPTIONS

The inner channel is mandatory. The ML-KEM-1024 + X25519 + PSK suite and
per-message AES-256-GCM keys cannot be disabled or peer-selected. Authenticated
bounded ratchet policies may widen the hybrid epoch budget without changing
those algorithms. There are no flags to select an inner mode, a hop layer, or a
transport Argon2 stage.

## HTTP FACADE AND OPERATOR IDENTITY OPTIONS

@options
@opt **--real**

Serve real HTTP for non-YUME requests on the same port.
@opt **--real-index** *path*
@cli spell: --real-index <path>
@cli help: HTML file for / (maximum 8 MiB)

HTML file served for **/**, limited to 8 MiB.
@opt **--real-root** *dir*
@cli spell: --real-root <dir>
@cli help: Serve GET/HEAD static files under <dir>
@cli help: (maximum 8 MiB per response)
@cli help: (implies --real; one web identity for
@cli help: HTTP/1.1 and the H2 decoy). Pair with
@cli help: --hide-in-the-crowd nginx for best fit.

Serve GET/HEAD static files under *dir* as the masquerade cover (implies
**--real**). Each response is limited to 8 MiB. Files are returned with the
correct MIME type, **Content-Length**, **Last-Modified**, an nginx-style
**ETag**, and **Accept-Ranges: bytes**; **/** and directory paths serve
*dir*/index.html. Path resolution rejects traversal, encoded-slash tricks,
control bytes, and every symlink component, including ancestors of the
configured root. POSIX directory descriptors pin resolution; platforms without
this support, including Windows, refuse static-root reads. Misses and
non-GET/HEAD methods return the profile 404. The same root backs the HTTP/1.1
probe and the H2 decoy. Pair with **--hide-in-the-crowd nginx** for the closest
header fit.
@opt **--real-secret-file** *path*
@cli spell: --real-secret-file <path>
@cli help: Cover-backend secret file; loaded, or created on first start
@cli column: 28

Owner-only file holding the cover-backend secret. It is read at start, or
created with fresh random contents when it does not exist. There is no inline
form: a secret passed on the command line or written into the configuration
file would be readable from the process table or the file, so **real_secret**
is refused by both configuration loaders.
@opt **--operator-identity**
@cli spell: --operator-identity
@cli help: Publish an operator identity proof and enable
@cli help: privacy-minimizing server behavior

Publish an operator identity proof and minimize identifying log fields where
supported. The proof authenticates CA-authorized operator control; it cannot
prove that the host does not inspect or retain traffic. This lifecycle belongs
to standalone **yumed-v2-reference**. Embedded servers, including the GUI and transport-v2
ABI backend, reject **anonym=true** at start.
@opt **--operator-proof-mode** *mode*
@cli spell: --operator-proof-mode <m>
@cli help: auto, local, or fixcraft
@cli column: 28

Proof policy: **auto**, **local**, or **fixcraft**.
@opt **--operator-proof-api** *url*
@cli spell: --operator-proof-api <url>
@cli help: External proof API URL (fixcraft mode)
@cli column: 29

External proof API URL, used by **fixcraft** proof mode.
@opt **--operator-proof-token-file** *path*
@cli file: yes
@cli spell: --operator-proof-token-file <path>
@cli help: Owner-only proof API token file (1-4096 bytes)
@cli column: 37

Owner-only file containing the external proof API token. The file must be a
regular non-symlink owned by the current user, have no group or world
permissions, contain 1 to 4096 bytes, and contain no HTTP control characters.
There is no inline configuration or command-line token form.
@opt **--operator-ca-key** *path*
@cli file: yes
@cli spell: --operator-ca-key <path>
@cli help: Operator CA private key

Operator CA private key.
@opt **--operator-ca-cert** *path*
@cli file: yes
@cli spell: --operator-ca-cert <path>
@cli help: Operator CA certificate
@cli column: 28

Operator CA certificate.
@opt **--operator-delegated-key** *path*
@cli file: yes
@cli spell: --operator-delegated-key <path>
@cli help: Delegated server identity key
@cli column: 34

Delegated server identity private key.
@opt **--operator-delegated-cert** *path*
@cli file: yes
@cli spell: --operator-delegated-cert <path>
@cli help: CA-signed delegated server certificate
@cli column: 35

CA-signed delegated server certificate. Its issuer should identify the operator
and its subject should identify the server name/alias.
@opt **--upstream-response** *path*
@cli spell: --upstream-response <p>
@cli help: Replay a pre-captured real HTTP/1.x response
@cli help: (maximum 8 MiB after line normalization)
@cli help: with complete HTTP framing; body bytes are kept.
@cli help: Header LF is accepted. Capture with
@cli help: `curl --http1.1 --raw -i https://real-site/notfound > resp.http`
@cli help: once and point this flag at it. Wins over
@cli help: --hide-in-the-crowd when both are set.

Serve a captured HTTP response to failed probes instead of the synthetic
profile-driven reply. Header LF endings are normalized to CRLF; body bytes and
chunk framing are preserved. Use **curl --http1.1 --raw -i** to retain transfer
framing. The capture must contain one complete HTTP/1.x final response;
malformed, conflicting, truncated, or trailing framing is refused. HTTP/2
conversion removes chunk framing before DATA emission. Replay is not equivalent
to a live upstream. Headers are limited to 64 KiB and the normalized response
to 8 MiB. Empty uses the synthetic profile.
@opt **--upstream-response-dir** *dir*
@cli spell: --upstream-response-dir <d>
@cli help: Like --upstream-response but loads every
@cli help: *.http / *.response in the directory and
@cli help: scans at most 4096 entries, accepts at most
@cli help: 256 captures of 8 MiB each, and caches at
@cli help: most 64 MiB total. It then
@cli help: picks one at random per probe. Avoids the
@cli help: simplest identical-capture replay check.
@cli help: Wins over --upstream-response when
@cli help: both are set.

Load every *\*.http* and *\*.response* file in *dir* and rotate between them
per probe, which avoids the "every probe gets the same capture" tell of a
single file. If both this and **--upstream-response** are set, the directory
wins. A reload scans at most 4096 directory entries, accepts at most 256
matching files, limits each normalized response to 8 MiB, and retains at most
64 MiB in aggregate.
@opt **--upstream-response-ttl** *seconds*
@cli spell: --upstream-response-ttl <s>
@cli help: When used with --upstream-response-dir, reloads
@cli help: the directory every <s> seconds so operators
@cli help: can drop new captures in without restarting.
@cli help: 0 = load once at startup (default).

With **--upstream-response-dir**, reload the directory every *seconds* so new
captures can be dropped in without restarting. 0 loads once at startup.
@end

